{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929302-very-confused-about-harmony-in-2-0","id":929302,"title":"Very Confused about Harmony in 2.0","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-10T11:50:34-07:00","id":929302,"title":"Very Confused about Harmony in 2.0","content":"So been reading more and more about Harmony and I now quite confused about how Harmony works, I am still more used to 1st edition and I do like the new mechanics with finding inner balance very interesting actually. But my issue is that is it now possible for a werewolf to just go insane, I did read that harmony 0 means that you are stuck in the shadow (Terrifying in my opinion) but how do breaking points work and at what level are they considered breaking points. Are feral werewolves still a thing or are they just not used anymore? I am sorry for my ignorance on the topic but I could not find any other information pertaining to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:01:27-07:00","id":929309,"title":"","content":"There aren't Zi'ir, unless the stacking amount of bans such an Uratha attains drives them to such abyss of insanity. Keep in mind that at extreme levels of harmony, sinning on the other spectrum is considerably easy. Force-feed burgers to your shadow entrapped packmate, it's only a matter of time before he starts to regain some Harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:13:29-07:00","id":929320,"title":"","content":"2e CofD's Integrity traits don't have as much association with mental health as 1e's Morality traits. There is still an association there, and an Uratha who balances in the middle around Harmony 5 is better adjusted to life as a werewolf than one at the extremes of flesh at Harmony 10 or spirit at Harmony 0. But the derangement system isn't used in 2e, and breaking points for Harmony don't accumulate negative Conditions, the way breaking points for other Integrity traits usually do. So no, I don't believe werewolves go unplayably mad simply from the violation of Harmony. They do, however, suffer behavioral restraints that make it harder to engage in healthy, reasoned interactions: as they drift from Harmony 5, more common and innocuous situations begin to risk the Death Rage, and as they break towards spirit below Harmony 5 they also accumulate bans. A werewolf with a passive Death Rage trigger and several bans doesn't look meaningfully different from a dangerous lunatic.<br /> <br /> There are two broad categories of breaking points for Harmony: the general and the extreme. You're always susceptible to triggering general breaking points, regardless of your current Harmony, whereas extreme breaking points only occur when you are at the edges (Harmony 3- or 8+). Each breaking point goes in a specific direction, either towards flesh or spirit, and extreme breaking points break away from their respective edges, meaning they are actually <i>good</i> for you, being easy ways you can harmonize yourself back towards the ideal Harmony 5. The best practice is thus, when you find yourself drifting towards the spirit (likely from being too kill-happy) or the flesh (likely from spending long periods of time keeping your human life healthy and active), to actively seek out breaking points to bounce yourself back in the opposite direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:30:56-07:00","id":929328,"title":"","content":"I like it but I miss the Feral werewolves, I mean I can probably still have an equivalent to them but the fact that Harmony 0 does not make the character unplayable is kind off a pisser in my opinion, I mean one can be stuck in the shadow and come back from that? I understand the idea is that it would be very hard to play a werewolf at low harmony but it seems to me like cheating still. My opinion may change as I run my campaign but that just seems odd to me in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:43:26-07:00","id":929334,"title":"","content":"Well, you're only trapped in the Shadow as long as your Harmony remains at 0, and it's still possible to experience Breaking Points toward Flesh, which will bring it back up if you fail them. So, for example, if your packmates buy a ton of McDonalds, bring it to the Shadow, and force you to eat it, you'll get Breaking Points towards Flesh for eating processed food, and might eventually fail one and gain a dot of Harmony. Or they could just kill your spiritual Touchstone, which causes an automatic +1 Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T13:03:29-07:00","id":929349,"title":"","content":"Harmony 10 is just as bad as 0 - playing a werewolf at either extreme isn't cheating, just hard!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T13:06:02-07:00","id":929354,"title":"","content":"Once you get to either end you have strange werewolves. At Harmony 10 a werewolf can't change without it costing Essence, and their methods of gaining Essence are slim. Plus with their Triggers they're going into death rage due to incidents around them that they couldn't have avoided if they wanted to. You can look at the Pack supplement to see how werewolves might deal with this. One pack is so devastated after the damage they inflicted during Kuruth that they've locked themselves up in solitary confinement completely separate from each other and their only contact with the outside world is through trusted wolf-blooded who might not be trustworthy much longer. The neurotic mess of a ghost wolf in the core book was a good example of a werewolf trying to resist their werewolf urges and cling to humanity.<br /> <br /> On the other end of the spectrum the low Harmony werewolves are going to be bundled with bans, as noted above. You may not think these are 'feral' werewolves, but they change instinctively every time they're stressed and can only resist it by spending Essence, also go into death rage at the drop of a hat, and their bans should be keeping them acting more erratic than the zi'ir of first edition.<br /> <br /> It's worth keeping in mind that these extremes aren't always going to be consequences for how you act. They might also be choices made by werewolves who either want to deny their true nature or escape their human side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-10-2016, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T19:21:58-07:00","id":929498,"title":"","content":"I think I am understanding more and more now but I have one more question, how is having harmony 8 or above a breaking point against spirit wouldn't that mean that there is always a chance to have your harmony decrease when harmony 10 just because now having 8 or above is a breaking point. same goes for having harmony 3 or below as a breaking point against flesh. Am I reading something wrong or is that how the rule works for those breaking points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T19:26:16-07:00","id":929500,"title":"","content":"You seem to have an old version of the pdf. It was fixed to show that you have some Breaking Points when your Harmony is above 8 or below 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T19:27:30-07:00","id":929501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929302-very-confused-about-harmony-in-2-0?p=929498#post929498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I am understanding more and more now but I have one more question, how is having harmony 8 or above a breaking point against spirit wouldn't that mean that there is always a chance to have your harmony decrease when harmony 10 just because now having 8 or above is a breaking point. same goes for having harmony 3 or below as a breaking point against flesh. Am I reading something wrong or is that how the rule works for those breaking points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you certain you have the most up-to-date version of the PDF? In the pre-errata version, there was a formatting error where &quot;Harmony 8 or above&quot; and &quot;Harmony 3 or below&quot; were accidentally listed as bullet points in the Harmony chart instead of headings. The bullet points listed below those headings only count as Breaking Points if your Harmony is above/below that threshold.<br /> <br /> You should check DrivethruRPG, you should be able to download the corrected version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-11-2016, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T19:31:46-07:00","id":929505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929302-very-confused-about-harmony-in-2-0?p=929501#post929501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you certain you have the most up-to-date version of the PDF? In the pre-errata version, there was a formatting era where &quot;Harmony 8 or above&quot; and &quot;Harmony 3 or below&quot; were accidentally listed as bullet points in the Harmony chart instead of headings. The bullet points listed below those headings only count as Breaking Points if your Harmony is above/below that threshold.<br /> <br /> You should check DrivethruRPG, you should be able to download the corrected version.</div> </div> </div> </div>yep that was the problem, thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T09:00:15-07:00","id":929768,"title":"","content":"You could totally have a werewolf that has gone totally feral and eats people for fun. There's just not a specific harmony level associated with it any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T09:09:14-07:00","id":929775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/929302-very-confused-about-harmony-in-2-0?p=929768#post929768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could totally have a werewolf that has gone totally feral and eats people for fun. There's just not a specific harmony level associated with it any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's entire lodges dedicated to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T09:10:05-07:00","id":929777,"title":"","content":"Or you could just have a non-feral one who eats people.<br /> <br /> There's probably some Conditions you could whip up for a werewolf who has abandoned society and the Oaths of the Moon and gone wild. One to offer a penalty to social interactions with humans and werewolves, take beats when it causes a significant setback. Bans are an easy way to get Beats, too.<br /> <br /> It's pretty easy to adapt some things to second edition. It helps that zi'ir weren't really anything concrete. Basically you have bans, easily done, eat flesh, also easily done, and are abandoned by Luna and totems. This isn't difficult to replicate if you find it really necessary, but the new system allows more variety and versatility while also allowing one to play a reluctant werewolf who pulls to either end of the spectrum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-11-2016, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}